	Section:
		Text: Text formatting
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Code
		Paragraph: With `Markup: markdown`, what goes between backticks is code and takes the font of `Code font`, usually a monospaced one. `Code font` is inherited, and these documents declare it once with `For element: Document`. A text with code and no `Code font` is an error.
			Style: intro
		Text: Run `mvn test` before publishing, and `mvn -o package` to build offline.
			Style: source
		Text: Run `mvn test` before publishing, and `mvn -o package` to build offline.
			Style: result
		Text: The code keeps the bold and the italic around it: **the `--force` flag** and *the `-v` flag*.
			Style: source
		Text: The code keeps the bold and the italic around it: **the `--force` flag** and *the `-v` flag*.
			Style: result
		Text: Code font: IBM Plex Serif  (any family can be the code font)
			Style: label
		Text: Run `mvn test` before publishing.
			Style: result
			Typography:
				Code font: IBM Plex Serif
